# Repository guidance for automated and human review.
#
# Replace `@dysshanks` with either your GitHub handle or a team handle. As teams are created
# under Settings -> Teams, the per-area owners below can become team references.
#
# CAUTION: if a handle or team in this file does not exist, GitHub silently assigns nobody and
# "Require review from Code Owners" becomes a no-op that still looks enabled in the settings UI.
# After editing this file, confirm a reviewer actually appears on a test pull request.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                       @dysshanks

# Architectural boundaries. A change here can invalidate the layering rules or the public API
# surface, so it needs a deliberate review, not just a passing build.
src/main/java/org/curioone/control/core/       @dysshanks
src/main/java/org/curioone/control/hardware/   @dysshanks
src/main/java/org/curioone/control/drive/      @dysshanks
src/main/java/org/curioone/control/math/       @dysshanks
src/main/java/org/curioone/control/control/    @dysshanks
src/main/java/org/curioone/control/util/       @dysshanks
src/main/java/org/curioone/control/command/    @dysshanks
src/main/java/org/curioone/control/telemetry/  @dysshanks
src/main/java/org/curioone/control/vision/     @dysshanks

# Build, CI, and publishing. A mistake here affects every consumer, and a mistake in the FTC
# SDK unpacking fails the build for everyone at once rather than for one reviewer.
build.gradle.kts                            @dysshanks
buildSrc/                                   @dysshanks
settings.gradle.kts                         @dysshanks
gradle/                                     @dysshanks
config/                                     @dysshanks
.github/                                    @dysshanks

# Architecture decisions. These govern everything else, so changes need explicit sign-off.
ARCHITECTURE_DECISIONS.md                   @dysshanks
docs/adr/                                   @dysshanks

# Release-critical files.
CHANGELOG.md                                @dysshanks
RELEASE_STRATEGY.md                         @dysshanks
